Born in Safad, northern Palestine, around 1888-[18]90, Ab[bo] was a farmer and fisherman who later took up carpentry and stone masonry. It was not until he moved to Berlin in 1911 to study sculpture that his artistic career took shape.
Baalbaki has spent the last four years finding[,] and determining attribution for, 70 artworks and 100 texts mentioning the artist.
