Telitz, 22, from Birch[wood,] Wis., put on another clinic during his Semi Final round. He made an exemplary start from the pole and led all 15 laps to ensure a place on the front row of the grid for the 20-lap Grand Final. He had to be content with the outside position, due to the[ fact] his Semi Final had been interrupted by two Safety Car periods which ensured a slower average speed than Semi Final 2[.] Undeterred, Telitz made a good start and immediately began to pressurize race leader Jonny McMullan.
